  <p><strong>Laravel</strong> is a full PHP application framework, not a set of pages you upload by FTP. It expects a real runtime: a recent PHP, several extensions, a writable storage directory, scheduled tasks and - for anything non-trivial - background queue workers. That's why basic shared hosting often fights you, and why a <strong>VPS</strong> is usually the right home for a Laravel app. This guide covers what the server actually needs and walks through a real deployment.</p>

